as a drunk it's his pragmatism and  compassion in the face of war that sets  him apart from his father at least in  the beginning he so believes his father  is wrong fighting the rebellious Hotspur  he puts his own life on the line to  challenge him in one-on-one combat  whoever wins decides the battle saving  countless lives  this selflessness  juxtaposed with Henry's brother Thomas  after Henry's victory against Hotspur he  says his field was mine it was to mark  my Dominion Thomas doesn't care at all  about the countless lives in blood that  was to be shed he only cares for his own  glory Henry on the other hand even  knowing he won't be king put his life on  the line it's when Henry becomes King  however that things start to change he's  no longer a drunk womanizer but on the  same token he's started to move slowly  away from being that strong moral  compass and that selflessness he's had  is starting to be manipulated by  external events around him  the first test comes in the form of a  ball a supposed present from the  delphine of France it's a cruel joke  suggesting the king to be a boy who  still plays with toys a gesture which  would make other Kings march off to  battle to defend their honor  not so with Henry even though he is  recommended to retaliate by his advisers  when this fails to provoke England to  war a new plot is devised an  assassination attempt is foiled twisting  Henry's arm to march on France leading  to their eventual victory at the Battle  of Agincourt during this time Henry's  compassion wanes he orders Falstaff to  kill the prisoners which when he refuses  almost ends up in killing his closest  friend and confidant don't dis about you  right here with my own hand  as his grip on power crumbles so too  does that young compassionate King to be  we saw in the beginning which leads us  to Henry's conversation one may even  liken it to an interrogation of his  future wife Catherine of Valois he asks  her about the assassination attempt and  she iterates that neither his father nor  his brother were the ones to order it in  fact she was in the room when her father  received a message accusing him of the  plot seeing his reaction of laughter at  the farcical claim Henry believes her to  be true therefore making the person  behind the plot someone within his inner  circle he interrogate slore Chief  Justice William asking him how much land  he sought to gain if England were to  conquer France a number he does not know  off the top of his head  Henry presses further asking him how he  came about knowing of this assassination  plot but his lies are easily seen  through that  Chief Justice confesses his part in the  plot saying that it was for the Kings  own good giving you what you wanted boy  am i all Henri wanted was peace but it  came at the costs of thousands of lives  not to mention Henry killing his own  cousin who he thought involved in the  assassination plot this is hope pieces  for it is forged in victory but victory  at the cost of war is never what Henry  wanted his entire conquest in France was  a manipulation  Henry had unwillingly become what he  hated most his father who lust for  conquest when William gets on his knees  to profess Henry's greatness he's  brutally stabbed and killed he is shown  no compassion this is all done before  the eyes of a child a symbol of  innocence Henry then visits Catherine  asking for only one thing from her that  she always speaks to him clear and true  the betrayal of the chief justice  someone who was supposed to speak clear  and true has made Henry wary if he's  going to embark on marriage with her he  needs her to promise this he longs for  truth and clarity which catherine says  she will give him it is said that both  Catherine and Henry loved each other in  real life however there's no evidence to  support that Henry murdered his chief  justice after finding out his  involvement in an assassination plot  that's the art of adapting a real  historical character into a film  adaptation you have to stretch facts in  order to create captivating character  arcs and structural plots  well the ending may not be entirely  accurate the movie isn't so much about  its ending but Henry's journey as a  character touching on themes of what it  means to be strong and what it means to  be a king Henry would go on to rule  until 14 22 roughly seven years after  the Battle of Agincourt paving the way  for more internal struggle within  England and the eventual victory of the  Hundred Years War by France I hope you  enjoyed this video please Knight me by  giving it a like and subscribing I have  more videos coming out every week you  can also follow me on Twitter at think  storyline  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much

